@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Toggletip}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Toggletip @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Toggletip @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</h1>


<p>
    ToggleTip (a term coined by Heydon Pickering) displays supplemental information on click, key press, touch or voice control rather than on on mouseover/hover.
</p>
<p>
    The component has been designed so it can be placed inline within a paragraph of text and unless overridden its label and icon will size accordingly. The label visibility is optional
    as its still used for the components accessible name. You can also reverse the ordering of the label and icon. As the component has a <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">RenderFragment</span>
    parameter for child content, you can include whatever html content you like.  You provide the content and set the desired size and position of the Toggletip and the component does the rest.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Important: </strong>The Toggletip component uses CSS anchor positioning with fallbacks for when it wont fit in the desired location which was only baseline at the start of the year 2026. Dependant on your target audience and supported browser versions,
    you may want to consider referencing the OddBird anchor positioning polyfill see: <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" target="_blank" href="https://github.com/oddbird/css-anchor-positioning">https://github.com/oddbird/css-anchor-positioning (opens in new window)</a>
    to support older browser versions. Without CSS anchor positioning the Toggletip content will be located at the top left of the page, but with all functionality intact.
</p>


<h2 style="margin-top:var(--br-unit-space-7)">Try the toggletip.</h2>
<p>
    The toggletip can be set apart from text or as in the example below just put inline with existing text. When using the default variable values the
    toggltips optional label and icon button will size to match. I have set the label (Keyboard info:) to be shown left of the icon, using the toggletip size of small.
    Not sure where it is, its the little icon buried in the lorum ipsum text. use the tab key to set focus on it.
</p>
<p>
    The toggletip uses light dismiss so clicking outside of the popover will close it, as will the escape key. The popover will remain open until closed, and as its not modal
    the user can tab out of the toggletip leaving it open. Opening an other item that uses the popover api, such as the Announcement History dialog will close an other open
    popover.
</p>
